  "generated_text": "1. The measure of each exterior angle of a regular polygon is $30$ degrees.\n2. The sum of the exterior angles in any polygon is $360$ degrees.\n3. For a regular polygon, each exterior angle is equal.\n4. To find the number of sides ($n$) of the polygon, we use the formula:\n   \\[\n   n = \\frac{360}{\\text{Exterior angle}} = \\frac{360}{30} = 12\n   \\]\n5. The sum of the interior angles in a polygon with $n$ sides is given by the formula:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Sum of interior angles} = (n-2) \\times 180\n   \\]\n6. Substitute $n = 12$ into the formula:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Sum of interior angles} = (12-2) \\times 180 = 10 \\times 180 = 1800\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the measures of the interior angles is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1800}\n\\]",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[1800, '1800']",
    "gold_answer": "Taking one exterior angle per vertex, the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is $360^\\circ$. If each exterior angle is $30^\\circ$, then the polygon has $\\frac{360}{30}=12$ sides. The sum of the interior angles of an $n$-sided polygon is $180(n-2)$, so for a polygon with 12 sides, the sum of the interior angles is $180(12-2)=\\boxed{1800}$ degrees.",
    "is_correct": true
  },
